{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 6, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "i recently watched \"the social network\" and was thoroughly impressed by the film's intricate storytelling, complex characters, and thought-provoking themes. directed by david fincher, the movie tells the story of facebook's founding and the subsequent rise of mark zuckerberg to fame and fortune.\n\nthe film begins with mark zuckerberg (played by jesse eisenberg), a sophomore at harvard, creating a website called \"facemash\" that allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. this initial success inspires mark to create a new website, \"thefacebook,\" with the help of his college roommates and fellow students eduardo savernin (andrew garfield), dustin moskovitz (josh pence), and chris hughes (patrick mapel).\n\nas the website gains popularity, mark becomes increasingly obsessed with expanding its user base and making it a success. however, this obsession comes at a cost, as he becomes embroiled in a series of lawsuits and feuds with his former friends and business partners. the film expertly weaves together multiple storylines, jumping back and forth between mark's time at harvard, his interactions with the Winklevoss twins (armie hammer), and the deposition hearings that follow.\n\none of the standout aspects of \"the social network\" is its cast. jesse eisenberg brings a nuanced and complex portrayal to mark zuckerberg, capturing both his intelligence and his awkwardness. andrew garfield is equally impressive as eduardo savernin, bringing a sense of vulnerability and charisma to the role. the chemistry between the two leads is undeniable, and their complicated friendship is at the heart of the film.\n\nthe supporting cast is equally impressive, with standout performances from justin timberlake as sean parker, the co-founder of napster, and brenda song as christy lee, a girl mark dates briefly. the film's score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is also noteworthy, perfectly capturing the mood and atmosphere of the film.\n\none of the most interesting aspects of \"the social network\" is its exploration of the themes of friendship, ambition, and the consequences of success. mark zuckerberg is a complex and multifaceted character, driven by a desire to succeed and a need for validation. as the film progresses, it becomes clear that mark's relationships with those around him are strained, and that his success comes at a significant personal cost.\n\noverall, \"the social network\" is a thought-provoking and engaging film that is well worth watching. with its intricate storytelling, complex characters, and nuanced exploration of themes, it is a movie that will stay with you long after the credits roll. if you're a fan of character-driven drama or are simply interested in the story of facebook's founding, \"the social network\" is a must-see.", "logprobs": [{"token": "i", "logprob": -1.883251667022705}, {"token": " recently", "logprob": -0.011960811913013458}, {"token": " watched", "logprob": -0.07889106869697571}, {"token": " \"", "logprob": -0.001604580320417881}, {"token": "the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " social", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "\"", "logprob": -0.018149960786104202}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.011054699309170246}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.22115755081176758}, {"token": " thoroughly", "logprob": -0.0015236446633934975}, {"token": " impressed", "logprob": -2.4199192921514623e-05}, {"token": " by", "logprob": -0.0015029336791485548}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.006789708510041237}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.0012347224401310086}, {"token": "'s", "logprob": -1.6689160474925302e-05}, {"token": " intricate", "logprob": -1.1717830896377563}, {"token": " storytelling", "logprob": -0.04952803626656532}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.07888974994421005}, {"token": " complex", "log